1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,777
Pick up any project where you left it.

2
00:00:03,127 --> 00:00:07,884
Its decisions, its source material and its next action, kept in files you own.

3
00:00:09,184 --> 00:00:16,224
Garrick is a workspace of plain files, run by the assistant you choose: Claude or Codex, in an app or a terminal.

4
00:00:16,524 --> 00:00:18,956
Every line of work keeps one resume point.

5
00:00:19,456 --> 00:00:20,907
SAM: Open launch plan.

6
00:00:26,712 --> 00:00:30,893
Calls and mail land in your inboxes. It files each one where it belongs.

7
00:00:31,293 --> 00:00:32,786
SAM: Process the inbox.

8
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:42,233
SAM: Both.

9
00:00:45,278 --> 00:00:51,529
Acme and Birch compete, so you've declared a wall between them. You met their carrier, Cobalt, once for each.

10
00:00:51,929 --> 00:00:53,252
SAM: Prep me for Cobalt.

11
00:01:00,025 --> 00:01:02,265
The Acme call stays out of Birch's brief.

12
00:01:02,565 --> 00:01:06,938
Walls are rules for the assistant, backed by limited checks before a commit.

13
00:01:08,138 --> 00:01:12,170
SAM: Board said March, and Theo's budget comes Wednesday. Wrap up.

14
00:01:16,425 --> 00:01:21,310
Tomorrow, Claude or Codex picks up from that note, not from a lost conversation.

15
00:01:22,510 --> 00:01:28,099
And an optional page, Garrick's Status, answers two questions: is anything wrong, and where was I?

16
00:01:29,399 --> 00:01:33,858
Your work, ready to pick up again, in files you own, with boundaries you declare.

17
00:01:34,358 --> 00:01:35,126
Garrick.
